webmscore 4.6.5-1 (partitioncloud/webmscore) built with emscripten 6.0.9 and Qt 6.10.3
instead of emsdk 3.1.14 and Qt 6.4.3:
- link flags: EXTRA_EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS is gone; export malloc/free as functions
  and HEAPU8 (no longer on Module by default) with the runtime methods
- link the offscreen platform plugin (built from source, see build.sh) instead of Qt's
  browser one; upstream CI deletes the wasm plugin's CMake files and drops in a
  prebuilt libqoffscreen.a
- load .mscx: MscReader reads it from the directory it is in, which a relative
  temporary file name ("XXXXXX.mscx") does not give ("File open error", also in the
  4.6.5-1 release); create the temporary file under QDir::tempPath()
- harfbuzz: its sources come from musescore/muse_deps, whose main branch no longer has
  harfbuzz/7.1.0; fetch them from the last commit that does
- freetype/brotli: add_subdirectory instead of subdirs(), which runs after Qt's
  deferred deployment-info call and makes it fail on the not yet read directories

diff --git a/buildscripts/cmake/SetupFreetypeBrotli.cmake b/buildscripts/cmake/SetupFreetypeBrotli.cmake
index c89f8fa..70d1ec8 100644
--- a/buildscripts/cmake/SetupFreetypeBrotli.cmake
+++ b/buildscripts/cmake/SetupFreetypeBrotli.cmake
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ add_compile_definitions(FT_CONFIG_OPTION_USE_BROTLI)
 
 include_directories(${MU_ROOT}/src/framework/draw/thirdparty/freetype)
 
-subdirs(
-    ${MU_ROOT}/thirdparty/brotli
-    ${MU_ROOT}/src/framework/draw/thirdparty/freetype
-)
+# add_subdirectory, not subdirs(): subdirs are only read after the top-level
+# CMakeLists, past Qt's deferred deployment-info call, which then cannot find them
+add_subdirectory(${MU_ROOT}/thirdparty/brotli brotli)
+add_subdirectory(${MU_ROOT}/src/framework/draw/thirdparty/freetype freetype)
